35,2,1,talk,Minato,,The treasurer logged six hours a month chasing individual payments.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The ledger shows seventy percent of costs are fixed, regardless of turnout.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,Nine tasters said they wouldn't commit to a whole year at once.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,Turnout fell by a third after we added door charges last summer.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,A quarter of members account for two-thirds of all attendances.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Ryuji, if costs are fixed, why do we charge per event?","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, because the fixed costs don't cover the variable ones.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@May, that explains the hesitation. People feel punished for missing out.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Minako, yes. The door charge made the evenings feel exclusive.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, so the heavy users are subsidizing the light ones?","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,I am worried about the administrative burden of tracking events.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,I am worried about setting a fee that is too low for the fixed costs.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,I am worried about scaring off the people who just want to drift in.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,I am worried about the social cost of making people count their steps.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,I am worried about the fairness of the current invisible subsidy.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,"A flat fee seems simplest for the books, but is it fair?","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"A flat fee covers the fixed costs, but ignores the variable ones.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minako,,A tiered system might let people choose their level of commitment.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,Activity-based charging feels too transactional for a social club.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,Tiered membership might formalize the difference between heavy and light users.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
